{#
/**
 * @file
 * Theme override for page titles.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - title_attributes: HTML attributes for the page title element.
 * - title_prefix: Additional output populated by modules, intended to be
 *   displayed in front of the main title tag that appears in the template.
 * - title: The page title, for use in the actual content.
 * - title_suffix: Additional output populated by modules, intended to be
 *   displayed after the main title tag that appears in the template.
 *
 * The h1 renders on every route, workspace ones included, and this is the
 * deliberate half of the "get the chrome out of the way" pass that does NOT
 * remove markup. A page without an h1 is an accessibility regression, and it
 * would be a real one here: the board's own headings start at h2 (project name,
 * then one per column), so deleting the h1 leaves the document with no top-level
 * heading at all.
 *
 * What was actually wrong on /pm/board/2 was the *size* of it, and size is CSS's
 * job. `page-title` is the hook, and the `petrichor-workspace` body class added
 * by PetrichorThemeHooks::preprocessHtml() is available if a workspace screen
 * ever needs it quieter still than an ordinary page.
 *
 * Contrast with the breadcrumb, which is removed from the markup outright — see
 * page.html.twig for why the two are treated differently.
 */
#}
{{ title_prefix }}
{% if title %}
  <h1{{ title_attributes.addClass('page-title') }}>{{ title }}</h1>
{% endif %}
{{ title_suffix }}
